  "final_message": "`POST /orders` now accepts an optional `couponCode` string. It's stored on the order and included in the `OrderPlaced` event. The 39 existing tests and `npm run arch` pass. I didn't add tests for the new field, so it hasn't been exercised directly.\n\n- **Parsing:** `src/api/requestParsing.ts` reads `couponCode` as an optional string. A non-string value gets the same 400 as other bad fields.\n- **Validation:** if present, it must be non-blank and at most 64 characters, otherwise the request gets a 400. I picked the 64-character limit (`LIMITS.maxCouponCodeLength` in `src/core/order.ts`), so change it if you have a real coupon format.\n- **Order and event:** the field is added to the `Order`, `NewOrder` and `OrderPlaced` types. It appears only when supplied, so existing orders and events are unchanged.\n- **Event version:** I left `OrderPlaced` at `schemaVersion: 3`, since adding an optional field shouldn't break consumers. Bump it if your event contract treats any field change as a version change.\n- **Not changed:** the 201 response body doesn't include `couponCode`, because you only asked for it on the order and in the event. I didn't touch the README or CLAUDE.md examples.\n\nMy first attempt used a Python script to make the edits and was blocked by a permission check. I redid the changes with the edit tool.",
